# dice_combinations:
# CSES 1633, Dice Combinations (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1633), in our
# own words: the number of sequences of dice throws, each 1 to 6, whose sum is
# total, modulo 10^9 + 7. Part of the CSES port's first batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: the list of all such sequences is
# built, from the running sum partial_sum = 0 upwards (no sequence once partial_sum > total, the empty
# sequence once partial_sum = total, otherwise each face put in front of the sequences of
# partial_sum + face), and its length is counted in binary and reduced modulo 10^9 + 7. Its
# reading is exponential in total even under tabling, since the sequences
# themselves are built and counted; the replacement the family asks for is
# the one-dimensional recurrence ways(partial_sum) = sum over face of ways(partial_sum + face) on
# fixed-width integers modulo 10^9 + 7.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ, application and
# top, with no choice and no parallel outside top. It β-reduces to V, the
# canonical binary numeral of the answer (every recursion consumes the bounded
# gap total - partial_sum, a finite list or a binary numeral): every top it holds (a bit of a
# literal that no key expects) stands in a branch that a Scott boolean discards,
# and binary_subtract, which writes no top (../common/binary_modular), is never
# asked for less than zero, since the program subtracts only what is no larger.
# So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the soundness of the derivable equations for the
# contextual preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W,
# while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to
# λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the
# second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons append map _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero binary_even binary_odd _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment merge_binary_plus _ merge_binary_equality
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "cses") "common") "binary_modular")
λ _ _ _ binary_modulo
. (λtuple. tuple λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd binary_zero)
λ modulus
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple λ. fixpoint λself function items. items nil λhead tail. append (function head) λ. self function tail
  )
λ concat_map
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple λ. fixpoint λself count items. items count λ_ tail. self (merge_binary_increment count) tail
  )
λ count_from
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
      ( cons (binary_odd binary_zero)
      λ
      . cons (binary_even λ. binary_odd binary_zero)
      λ
      . cons (binary_odd λ. binary_odd binary_zero)
      λ
      . cons (binary_even λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd binary_zero)
      λ
      . cons (binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd binary_zero)
      λ
      . cons (binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_odd binary_zero) nil
      )
  )
λ faces
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ total
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self partial_sum
        . binary_less_than total partial_sum nil λ. merge_binary_equality partial_sum total (cons nil nil) λ. concat_map (λface. map (cons face) λ. self λ. merge_binary_plus partial_sum face) faces
      ) binary_zero
  )
λ sequences
. (λtuple. tuple λtotal. binary_modulo (count_from binary_zero λ. sequences total) modulus)
λ dice_combinations
. export dice_combinations
